      feat: semgrep pattern extensions for Scala
      
      Adds semgrep-scala, extending the tree-sitter-scala grammar with
      semgrep pattern constructs: metavariables ($FOO), ellipsis (...),
      named ellipsis ($...ARGS), and deep expressions (<... e ...>).
      
      Grammar extensions (common/semgrep-ext.js):
      - __SEMGREP_EXPRESSION, __SEMGREP_STATEMENT, __SEMGREP_MEMBER_DECL
        sentinel tokens as top-level entry points
      - semgrep_metavariable, semgrep_ellipsis, semgrep_ellipsis_metavariable,
        deep_expression as new terminal/rule types
      - _simple_expression extended to allow semgrep constructs in expression
        positions (arguments, bodies, infix operands, etc.)
      - _pattern extended for ellipsis in case class and tuple patterns
      - parameter and class_parameter extended for ellipsis in parameter lists
      - enumerator extended for ellipsis between for-comprehension generators
      
      Scanner fix (src/scanner.c):
      - AUTOMATIC_SEMICOLON suppression for '.' is refined to only suppress
        when '.' is followed by a non-dot character (i.e., a method chain).
        '...' at line-start now correctly triggers semicolon insertion,
        matching the approach used in semgrep-kotlin.
      
      Test corpus covers definitions, disambiguation, expressions, patterns,
      statements, and real-world security/taint patterns.
      
